ALCF patch 0001: bind accelerators by node-local rank, not global rank

Upstream (collective_perf_test.py, PR #2633 @ 157738b) does:

    torch.accelerator.set_device_index(rank % device_count)

using the GLOBAL rank. That is only correct when ranks-per-node happens to
equal devices-per-node. On a 12-tile PVC node:

    2 nodes x 12 rpn  -> correct by accident (12 % 12 wraps to 0)
    2 nodes x  2 rpn  -> WRONG: ranks 2,3 bind tiles 2,3 instead of 0,1
    2 nodes x  6 rpn  -> WRONG: ranks 6..11 bind tiles 6..11 instead of 0..5

We observed this live in our Phase 2 smoke run (Ranks=4 = 2 nodes x 2 rpn).
The benchmark still completes, so the failure is silent: you get numbers for
a tile pairing you did not ask for.

The fix reads a node-local rank from the environment, preferring LOCAL_RANK
(exported by tc-perf-env, and by torchrun) and falling back through the PALS,
Intel MPI, OpenMPI and Slurm spellings. If none is present it returns the
global rank, which is exactly upstream's behaviour -- so this patch cannot
make an un-wrapped run worse.

Not upstreamed: PR #2633 is a draft we assume will not merge.

--- a/collective_perf_test.py
+++ b/collective_perf_test.py
@@ -58,6 +58,37 @@
 REDUCE_OPS = ["sum", "min", "max", "avg", "product"]
 
 
+# --- ALCF patch 0001 -------------------------------------------------------
+# Node-local rank discovery. torchcomms' own get_rank_and_world_size() checks
+# OMPI_COMM_WORLD_*, RANK/WORLD_SIZE, SLURM_*, PMI_* -- none of which PALS sets
+# for the LOCAL rank, and the harness has no local-rank concept at all. The
+# perf_env wrapper exports LOCAL_RANK, so prefer that; the rest are fallbacks
+# for running under a different launcher without the wrapper.
+_LOCAL_RANK_ENV_VARS = (
+    "LOCAL_RANK",               # torchrun, and our tc-perf-env wrapper
+    "PALS_LOCAL_RANKID",        # PBS/PALS (Aurora, Sunspot)
+    "MPI_LOCALRANKID",          # Intel MPI
+    "OMPI_COMM_WORLD_LOCAL_RANK",
+    "SLURM_LOCALID",
+)
+
+
+def _local_rank_from_env(fallback: int = 0) -> int:
+    """Node-local rank, or `fallback` (the global rank) if nothing says.
+
+    Falling back to the global rank reproduces upstream's behaviour exactly,
+    so an un-wrapped run is no worse off than before this patch.
+    """
+    for var in _LOCAL_RANK_ENV_VARS:
+        val = os.environ.get(var)
+        if val is not None and val.strip() != "":
+            try:
+                return int(val)
+            except ValueError:
+                pass
+    return fallback
+
+
 VALUE_FLAGS = {
     "--warmup",
     "--iters",
@@ -282,7 +313,15 @@
         if torch.accelerator.is_available():
             device_count = torch.accelerator.device_count()
             if device_count > 0:
-                torch.accelerator.set_device_index(rank % device_count)
+                # ALCF patch 0001: bind by NODE-LOCAL rank, not global rank.
+                # Upstream uses `rank % device_count`, which is only correct
+                # when ranks-per-node == devices-per-node. At 2 nodes x 2 ranks
+                # on a 12-tile node, ranks 2 and 3 land on tiles 2 and 3 of the
+                # second node while ranks 0 and 1 use tiles 0 and 1 of the
+                # first -- different tiles, so the measured path is not the
+                # one you asked for. Observed live in our Phase 2 run.
+                local_rank = _local_rank_from_env(rank)
+                torch.accelerator.set_device_index(local_rank % device_count)
 
         if rank == 0 and not record.config.quiet:
             print("Collective Performance Test")
